 "kit": "A Warden: layered bark plates on the shoulders, the arms and the legs, with leather bracers so that little skin shows; over the body armour a sleeveless surcoat of deep bottle-green cloth that covers his whole chest and belly (no bark plates over it) from the collar down to just below the knees, front and back, split at the front below the belt and held at the waist by a dark leather belt; a helm of bark plates with a tall crest of stiff deep green leaves running front to back, no antlers (antlers are a captain's mark, never a soldier's); a deep green mantle of overlapping cloth leaves thrown over both shoulders and the upper back; a round shield of bark-covered wood whose whole face is painted solid deep green with only a small pale blossom sigil at its centre and a thin bark-brown rim; a straight leaf-bladed sword; bark-brown weathered skin.",
